WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:03.300
-Our next guest is a very funny
comedian whose stand-up special

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.734
"Cold Lasagne Hate Myself 1999"

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:08.467
was recently nominated
for a Critics' Choice Award.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:10.467
Please welcome to the show
James Acaster.

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:11.901
How are you, James?

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:13.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.601
-Very well. Thank you, Seth.
So good to see you.

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:20.534
-My only regret is that
we're not meeting in person.

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:24.067
Is it safe to assume that
you're Zooming in from London?

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.367
-That is not safe to assume.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:29.767
Actually, I'm in a little place
called New York City!

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:31.400
Make some noise!

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:36.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.434
-But you're not here.

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:42.467
-No, I'm in a little place
called 29 Rockefeller Center.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:43.801
-Okay.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:47.000
-That is where I spend
a lot of my time in New York.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.300
I'm loyal to that building.
I will not set foot in 30 Rock.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.567
I'm 29 Rock till I die!

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:53.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:56.434
-You have long been
a supporter of 29 Rock.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:59.667
It's a very overlooked building,
so I totally understand.

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:02.267
-[ Laughter ]
-29 Rock forever.

00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:05.667
You can watch "Sunday Night
As Live," my favorite show.

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:08.567
It goes out every week.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:12.434
Hey, congratulations
on your special, which I adored.

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:15.067
It is chock-full of jokes.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:19.734
It also talks a lot about
the last few years of your life.

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:23.167
And it's two hours,
and it flies by.

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:24.801
You must be pleased
with the fact

00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:28.000
that it was nominated
for a Critics' Choice Award.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.601
-That's very kind of you.

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:31.567
Yeah, I am very pleased, excited
about the Critics' Choice Award.

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:34.067
Also, you know,
I like to get my hopes up.

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:37.300
It came out the same year
as "Inside," by Bo Burnham,

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:40.868
so I can just chill out
and let whatever happens happen,

00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:43.834
which I think we know
what's gonna happen.

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:46.033
The last special
I released was 2018,

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:47.334
which was the same year

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:49.067
that Hannah Gadsby released
"Nanette."

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:51.868
I have a rule
that I only release specials

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:54.901
when geniuses completely
reinvent the genre.

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:58.667
And then that's when
I drop something.

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:00.434
'Cause the pressure is off.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.100
-One thing I would say,

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.901
none of them
have anything on you,

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:08.601
as far as coming up with a title
as inventive as yours.

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:10.367
How did you come up with
this title?

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:12.901
Because I don't think anybody
else, any other comedian,

00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:16.167
would have dared
called a special this.

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:17.801
-They wouldn't have dared.
They're all too scared.

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:21.434
And, unlike me, they didn't have
the experience that I had

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:24.067
when I had a microwave lasagne,

00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:26.167
and it was hot
and it tasted rubbish.

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:28.701
So I put it in the fridge,
then I watched "Queer Eye"

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:31.300
and I got drunk,
and then at 3:00 in the morning,

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:34.767
I was so drunk and teary
after watching "Queer Eye"

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:36.934
that the idea of eating
the cold lasagne

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:39.267
was actually appealing to me.
I ate that.

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:41.167
It was the most delicious thing
I've ever tasted.

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:43.501
Like, all the béchamel sauce
kind of congeals

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:46.968
and has a foamy Haribo
sweet texture to it.

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:49.200
It's very good.
And then I got on a text group.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.534
It was 3:00 in the morning.

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:52.667
No one else is awake,
so I've got to do a solo.

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:54.801
They're my favorite times
to go on the text group,

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:56.167
is when you get to do a jazz --

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:59.167
Like, just complete
stream-of-consciousness solo

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:00.801
and tell them everything
that's on your mind,

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:02.133
but not in one block.

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:04.667
In loads of little short jabs,

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:06.133
each thought
as it occurs to you.

00:03:06.133 --> 00:03:09.067
And I just was like,
"Cold lasagne is delicious!

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:10.334
It's the best thing ever!

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:11.767
This is the happiest day
of my life!

00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:13.734
The best year of my life
was 1999."

00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:15.400
And then I started going,
"I hate myself.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.968
And I've just realized
how much I hate myself."

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:18.501
'Cause the drunkenness
kicked in.

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:20.501
And then I changed
the group name

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:24.801
to "Cold Lasagne Hate Myself
1999," passed out.

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:27.267
Then the next morning,
my agent texted me, saying,

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:28.567
"We need to name the show,

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.434
'cause the tickets
go on sale tomorrow,"

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:33.934
so I just gave them the most
recent name I'd come up with.

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:37.400
[ Laughter ] -

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.467
Bravo, bravo.

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:40.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:42.901
Now...

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:45.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:51.133
Some who might not know
your incredible work

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:53.267
as a stand-up
might have first discovered

00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:57.367
you when you were on
"Great British Bake Off."

00:03:57.367 --> 00:04:02.033
You had a -- You were a meme.
You know this now.

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:04.067
-I know this now.
-You know this now.

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:06.434
It was, "Started making it.

00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:09.334
Had a breakdown. Bon appetit."

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:12.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.234 --> 00:04:13.434
And, now, this was -- you --

00:04:13.434 --> 00:04:16.501
I heard you sort of blamed this
on America,

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:20.000
because this was
jet-lag-induced.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.267
-Yeah, I was coming back
from America.

00:04:21.267 --> 00:04:22.534
I was jet-lagged.

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:23.968
And then it turned out
to be the first thing

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:25.634
that got me known in America.

00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:27.234
Also, what you guys
don't know is,

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:31.234
all the memes that you love
are comedians abroad.

00:04:31.234 --> 00:04:34.300
That's what you guys don't know,
is that ---

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.000
That meme of the baby?
Just like that?

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:41.767
That is a really edgy comic
from Scandinavia, that baby,

00:04:41.767 --> 00:04:45.434
who makes Bill Burr
look like a wimp!

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:47.100
-They're all --
-They're all -- All the memes

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.200
are comedians abroad
who you guys haven't heard of.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:50.767
That's why the memes
are so funny.

00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:53.033
-[ Laughter ]
-But, yeah, I was jet-lagged,

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:56.434
so I did really bad on
"Great British Bake Off."

00:04:56.434 --> 00:04:57.734
And then when I said to them,

00:04:57.734 --> 00:04:59.467
"Started making it,
had a breakdown, bon appetit,"

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:01.367
I was not lying.
That was the truth.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.267
And then you lot laughed at it,

00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:04.667
and it was your fault
to begin with,

00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:06.534
'cause your country's
too far away.

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:08.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:10.467
-You've done a lot
of panel shows in England,

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:12.067
a lot of chat shows.

00:05:12.067 --> 00:05:17.467
What was your first talk-show
experience here in the States?

00:05:17.467 --> 00:05:19.901
-Ever heard of a gentleman
called Conan?

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:21.968
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:24.234
-Conan O'Brien, his name is.

00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:25.734
Real piece of work.

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:27.667
-[ Light laughter ]
-Real piece of work.

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:28.901
I'm glad he's off the air now.

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:30.667
I can't remember
what happened to him,

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:32.501
but he deserves
everything he gets.

00:05:32.501 --> 00:05:35.968
I went on his show,
and it went bad.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:38.868
And also, the night before,

00:05:38.868 --> 00:05:43.133
I had visited a Mexican
food truck in L.A.,

00:05:43.133 --> 00:05:45.734
and I didn't ask anyone

00:05:45.734 --> 00:05:48.367
for tips of which truck
to go to beforehand.

00:05:48.367 --> 00:05:50.133
And let's just say

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:53.000
that when I was on Conan's show,
doing the stand-up,

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.300
some of my insides were trying
to burst into my outsides.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:59.100
And within --

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.701
And bear in mind,
the audience didn't know this,

00:06:01.701 --> 00:06:04.634
but they could sense it --
because no laughs.

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:07.000
They weren't on my side.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:10.501
And then, within half an hour
of being on the show --

00:06:10.501 --> 00:06:12.701
and I wish this was a lie --

00:06:12.701 --> 00:06:14.801
I went to a steakhouse
and [bleep] my pants.

00:06:14.801 --> 00:06:17.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.834 --> 00:06:19.167
Like, literally [bleep] my --

00:06:19.167 --> 00:06:22.601
Not I went to a steakhouse
and then got scared of,

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:25.367
like, "Oh, what about
when that airs?"

00:06:25.367 --> 00:06:27.667
I literally did a [bleep]
in my pants.

00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:31.100
Like, it came out of my butt
and into my pants.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.234
The last place
I wanted it, Seth.

00:06:33.234 --> 00:06:35.968
-[ Laughter ]
-Last place I wanted it.

00:06:35.968 --> 00:06:37.868
I wanted it either
to stay in my butt

00:06:37.868 --> 00:06:40.567
or to find a new home
in a toilet.

00:06:40.567 --> 00:06:44.267
I didn't want it
in the pants I was wearing,

00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:47.367
which, by the way,
in the U.K. is underwear.

00:06:47.367 --> 00:06:51.467
But in this case,
the [bleep] got on both.

00:06:51.467 --> 00:06:54.300
So actually, to be fair,

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:57.601
it was a moment that
translated across the ocean.

00:06:57.601 --> 00:07:00.133
-Yeah.
-I [bleep] --

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:03.100
I [bleep] both things.
And that's Conan's fault.

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:04.767
And I'm glad that he's now --

00:07:04.767 --> 00:07:08.100
I'm glad that he will
never be on TV again,

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:12.501
because his show
made me [bleep] myself.

00:07:12.501 --> 00:07:16.200
-Well, I think one thing
we can agree on, I hope,

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:20.367
at least in your estimation,
this has gone better than that.

00:07:20.367 --> 00:07:22.200
-Yeah. Oh, I'm here.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:24.100
And you can't see,
'cause it's like this,

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:26.534
but I am just sat on the toilet
just in case.

00:07:26.534 --> 00:07:30.200
-[ Laughter ]
-Better safe than sorry.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.467
-Fool me once, Seth.

00:07:32.467 --> 00:07:34.667
-Hey, thanks so much!

00:07:34.667 --> 00:07:37.801
I really do hope
next time is in person.

00:07:37.801 --> 00:07:39.767
-I do, as well.
You're a lovely man.

00:07:39.767 --> 00:07:43.767
-James Acaster, everybody.
"Cold Lasagne Hate Myself 1999"

00:07:43.767 --> 00:07:45.968
is available to purchase
on Vimeo.

